---
import Lab from '../layouts/Lab.astro';

const work = [
  ['Agent surface', '`nf mcp`: a stdio MCP server over the headless engine. Read the part and its faces by name, set parameters or patch the program with JSON Patch, measure exact volume, area, centroid and bounds, export STEP and meshes. Every edit is rebuilt; a failed feature rolls back; every error carries a JSON Pointer into the document', 'in review'],
  ['Agent evaluation', 'every reference part built from its description, edited and repaired by an agent through `nf mcp`, then measured against the exact part. First run: 60 of 60 within 1e-6 in volume and area, median 7 turns per task', 'in review'],
  ['Feature program', 'a JSON feature list with named parameters and units, selectors instead of face indices, content hashes so one parameter change rebuilds only what it touches', 'shipped'],
  ['Kernel', 'OpenCASCADE 7.9.3 behind an XPC service with a watchdog; Rust owns the math, the ownership rules and the policy; exact STEP AP242 out', 'shipped'],
  ['Sketcher', 'a permissive Rust constraint solver owns the constraints; the agent proposes relations and reads degrees of freedom, conflicts and redundancy back. A measured spike picked SolidCraft\'s solver over ezpz on diagnostics', 'next'],
  ['Assemblies', 'components and occurrences, one frame-based joint per pair that carries its degrees of freedom, a small SE(3) solver, interference and clearance, URDF out so MuJoCo or Chrono can test the mechanism', 'planned'],
  ['Studies', 'structural, thermal and fluid studies as objects in the document, run out of process on permissive solvers, gated by analytic cases before anything is called a result', 'planned'],
  ['macOS app', 'SwiftUI and a Metal viewport: parameters, history, rollback and exact measures today; interactive sketching after the solver', 'preview'],
];

const status = [
  ['Direction', 'RFC 0011', 'the AI design loop program, in review: agent surface first, then sketch solver, assemblies and studies'],
  ['Platforms', 'macOS 15+', 'Apple Silicon; the headless engine and `nf` CLI build without the app'],
  ['License', 'Apache-2.0', 'OpenCASCADE is LGPL-2.1 and dynamically linked; no GPL code is linked'],
  ['Kernel decision', 'RFC 0001', 'bake-off on a 20-part corpus and 200 ABC models: OCCT 77.4 vs SMLib 50.7; SMLib stays buildable for re-evaluation'],
  ['Evidence', '899 tests', 'the occt gate, including the agent evaluation\'s reference run; every headless build returns a factual record: volumes, areas, digests, cache activity, timings'],
  ['FreeCAD', 'oracle', 'an earlier fork direction was retired; FreeCAD runs as a separate program to compute reference values for tests'],
];
---

<Lab
  path="/"
  current="overview"
  og="/og/nightfall.png"
  description="Nightfall is AI-native CAD for macOS: exact NURBS geometry, a feature program as the source of truth, and an agent that edits the program, rebuilds and measures every change."
>
  <h1>nightfall</h1>
  <p class="lede">AI-native CAD. Every part is a program; the agent edits the program, never the geometry, and every edit is rebuilt and measured.</p>

  <div class="actions">
    <a class="button button--primary" href="https://github.com/wckdboy/nightfall" rel="noopener">Source</a>
    <a class="text-link" href="/#work">The work</a>
    <a class="text-link" href="/brand/">Brand</a>
  </div>

  <dl class="facts">
    <div><dt>Geometry</dt><dd>exact NURBS</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Kernel</dt><dd>OpenCASCADE</dd></div>
    <div><dt>State</dt><dd>preview</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Telemetry</dt><dd>none</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <section id="why">
    <h2>Why a program, not a mesh</h2>
    <p>Text-to-3D gives you a mesh nobody can edit. Nightfall gives the agent the same thing a good engineer keeps: a feature program with named parameters, units and references that survive edits. The agent reads it, changes it, and gets back what actually happened: which bodies changed, their exact volume and area, and a pointer to the field that failed. That loop, write then run then measure then revise, is what makes an AI a useful co-worker in CAD, and it is the part most tools leave out.</p>
    <p>The rules do not change. Math is the source of truth and meshes are derived. Every part is a program: a feature list with named parameters, geometry as a cache. The agent edits the program, never the geometry. Built for making real things: millimetres, explicit tolerances, STEP, 3MF and SVG out. Rebuild status is never the verdict; measured geometry is.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="work">
    <h2>The work</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>What</th><th>State</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {work.map(([area, what, state]) => (
            <tr><td><strong>{area}</strong></td><td>{what}</td><td class="small">{state}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="small">Order of work: the agent loop first, with an evaluation suite over the reference parts, then the sketch solver, then assemblies and studies. The kernel keeps improving behind them; it is never the thing the loop waits on.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="status">
    <h2>Status</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <tbody>
          {status.map(([part, state, note]) => (
            <tr><td><strong>{part}</strong></td><td>{state}</td><td class="small">{note}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="small">The headless engine, the `nf` CLI and the macOS preview exist and are tested; the agent surface is in review; assemblies and studies are plans with written gates. The state column says what exists.</p>
  </section>
</Lab>
